*.psd filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Video is NOT stored in LFS.
#
# It was, and the homepage reel broke because of it. Vercel served the 133-byte
# pointer file instead of the video: the browser got `version
# https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1` where it expected an ftyp atom, and the
# player sat there dead. The previous production build had resolved the object
# fine, so this surfaced only on the next deploy — long after the commit that
# caused it.
#
# LFS was never earning anything here anyway. The 133 MB of jpgs under IMAGES/
# and Gallery/ are plain git blobs; only *.mp4 was singled out, which made the
# videos the one asset class whose delivery depended on the build host fetching
# a second protocol correctly. `binary` keeps git from attempting any
# line-ending conversion on them.
*.mp4 binary
